// `std.fs`: the home of the filesystem's host interface, `std.fs.Eff`, whose
// operations read and change files under a directory capability. A source
// names the interface where it imports this module, `import std.fs;`, and
// nowhere else. The interface is native, so no declaration here
// states it. The functions over a directory capability wait for demand.
//
// Its seam is `cap_std::fs::Dir`, `cap_tempfile::TempDir`,
// `cap_primitives::fs::open_dir`, which resolves beneath its start, and rustix
// `fs`.
//
// - see: #4523
// - see: `corpus/model/builtins/host-modules.gandr` and
//   `corpus/model/control/capability-attenuate.gandr` — the sources that use
//   the interface
